      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs(signal): document --signal-number, --http-host, --http-port CLI flags",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using `openclaw channels add --channel signal` with CLI flags had no documentation explaining what `--signal-number`, `--http-host`, and `--http-port` do.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Signal channel plugin declares these three flags in `package.json` (`cliAddOptions`) so the non-interactive setup wizard accepts them, but `docs/channels/signal.md` did not mention them. Each flag now has a one-line description and the default value where applicable, matching the existing channel documentation pattern used by googlechat.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can now look up what each Signal CLI flag does directly in the docs instead of trial-and-error or reading source code.\n\n## Evidence\n\nDocs-only change. The flag names, descriptions, and default values are verified against:\n\n- `extensions/signal/package.json` — `cliAddOptions` declarations\n- `docs/channels/signal.md` — existing config field docs (lines 73, 168, 421) confirm `127.0.0.1:8080` defaults",
        "branch": "fix/docs-cli-flags-missing",
